\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Thou to whom the sick and  dying
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0 Ever came, nor came in vain,
\par still with healing words replying
\par To the wearied cry of pain,
\par Hear us, Jesus, as we meet,
\par Suppliants at Thy mercy-seat.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. Still the weary, sick, and dying
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0 Need a brother's sister's care;
\par On thy higher help relying,
\par May we now their burden share
\par Bringing all our offerings meet,
\par Suppliants at Thy mercy-seat.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. May each child of Thine be willing,
\par \pard\li360\sl202\slmult0 willing both in hand and Heart,
\par All the law of love fulfilling,
\par Ever comfort to impart,
\par Ever bringing offerings meet,
\par Suppliants at Thy mercy-seat.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li360\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4. So may sickness, sin, and sadness
\par \pard\li360\sl202\slmult0 To Thy healing virtue yield,
\par Till the sick and sad, in gladness,
\par Rescued, ransomed, cleansed, healed,
\par one in Thee together meet,
\par \pard      Pardoned at Thy judgment-seat.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

